UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 29, Lesson 2: Digital time and 12-hour time', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Digital time shows hours and minutes with a colon (for example 09:05). Match digital displays to analog clock faces in 12-hour time.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nWrite digital for: minute hand on 2, hour near 7. Draw analog for 4:50.\n\nFEEDBACK\n7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5.\n\nWATCH FOR\nWriting 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nMatch ten digital↔analog pairs. Convert eight times both ways. Correct three invalid digital times and write why each fails.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"Digital time shows hours and minutes with a colon (for example 09:05). Match digital displays to analog clock faces in 12-hour time.","lesson_number":2,"lesson_role":"Strategies","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA2-NSM-02"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Match ten digital↔analog pairs. Convert eight times both ways. Correct three invalid digital times and write why each fails. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: 7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5. Reasoning: I used digital by attending to 12-hour and explain why it matters rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Writing 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59. Correction: 7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5. Why: the correction restores accurate use of digital.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Writing 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Solve one fresh problem that uses digital with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Describe one likely mistake with digital, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require new numbers, visible working and named places/values. / Require a real misconception, corrected working and a method reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5. This matches the lesson skill for digital.","options":["Copy the worked example and call it independent work.","7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5.","Writing 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59.","Ignore the task and invent an unrelated answer."],"question":"Write digital for: minute hand on 2, hour near 7. Draw analog for 4:50. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Writing 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59. That misconception weakens accuracy; the other choices align with the lesson idea.","options":["Writing 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59.","Digital time shows hours and minutes with a colon (for example 09:05). Match digital displays to analog clock faces in 12-hour time.","7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5.","Careful use of 12-hour and explain why it matters with clear evidence."],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when practising digital?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and named 12-hour and explain why it matters, not by copying the model.","options":["Treat a missing detail as a proven fact.","Apply the idea with new evidence and name the 12-hour and explain why it matters used.","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence.","Choose randomly because any option could be right."],"question":"A learner is practising digital. Which approach best shows understanding?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Mathematics answers need labelled working tied to place value or quantity.","options":["Show the places, values or steps and say why each step is valid.","Write only a final number with no working.","Change digits to look neater without checking place value.","Writing 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59."],"question":"Which working note best supports a mathematics answer about digital?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the method; the others break it.","options":["Writing 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59.","Ignore the task and invent an unrelated answer.","Copy the worked example and call it independent work.","7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5."],"question":"Using this lesson idea — Digital time shows hours and minutes with a colon (for example 09:05). Match digital displays to analog… — which statement is true?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Disagreement is resolved by checking places, operations and the question focus.","options":["Pick the longer-looking working automatically.","Delete units so the answers appear to match.","Average the two answers without checking either.","Recheck places,