nutes only go 00–59. Correction: 7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5. Why: the correction restores accurate use of digital.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent working and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-mat-y3-w29-l2","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA mathematics alignment using verified outcome code wording where recorded in lesson-pipeline/sources; content-point mapping remains pending.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise digital.","Read the mission before you start calculating.","Keep the place or unit you are working with in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your working with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the place or distance that carries the method.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore place value or working.","Prefer accurate method over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your working and reason are both present.","Proofread digits, places and operation signs.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact place, value or distance before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key numbers.","Say what each number represents in the method.","A final answer alone is weaker than labelled working."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with stronger working.","Change the value or method, not only how neat it looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose fresh numbers that still use the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original working and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new numbers."]},"subject":"Measurement and Space","success_criteria":["I can use digital with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify 12-hour and explain why it matters.","I can practise colon independently on a new prompt.","I can notice match needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Digital time shows hours and minutes with a colon (for example 09:05). Match digital displays to analog clock faces in 12-hour time. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence.","options":["Digital time shows hours and minutes with a colon (for example 09:05). Match digital displays to analog clock faces in 12-hour time.","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no working."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about digital?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\n2:45 digital matches an analog clock with minute hand on 9 (45 minutes) and hour hand near 3. 09:05 means 9 hours and 5 minutes.\n\nTRY FIRST\nWrite digital for: minute hand on 2, hour near 7. Draw analog for 4:50.\n\nFEEDBACK\n7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5.","explain":"Digital time shows hours and minutes with a colon (for example 09:05). Match digital displays to analog clock faces in 12-hour time.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Digital matched to analog.","caption":"Minutes only go 00–59.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Digital</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">2:45</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Analog</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">minute on 9</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: 2:45 digital matches an analog clock with minute hand on 9 (45 minutes) and hour hand near 3. 09:05 means 9 hours and 5  Then write your own working.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.\nJuno: Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: 2:45 digital matches an analog clock with minute hand on 9 (45 minutes) and hour hand near 3. 09:05 means 9 hours and 5  Then write your own working."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence.","options":["A calculation unrelated to the numbers given.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no working.","Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about digital?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\n2:45 digital matches an analog clock with minute hand on 9 (45 minutes) and hour hand near 3. 09:05 means 9 hours and 5 minutes. Look at each number, place or distance that carries the method.\n\nTRY FIRST\nWrite the key numbers from the model and say what each one represents in the method.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful working names the quantities and the reason for each step, not only the final answer.","explain":"Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing only the final answer without working does not show the method. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Show the working","visual":[{"alt":"Digital time with a leading zero.","caption":"Invalid times need correcting.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Also</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">09:05</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Means</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">9 hours 5 minutes</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific mathematical error, then show the corrected working. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence.","options":["A calculation unrelated to the numbers given.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no working.","Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific mathematical error, then show the corrected working."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about digital?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nWriting 7:70 as a time is impossible — minutes only go 00–59. Here is a more productive model: 2:45 digital matches an analog clock with minute hand on 9 (45 minutes) and hour hand near 3. 09:05 means 9 hours and 5 minutes.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDescribe why the warned-against approach gives the wrong value or meaning, then write corrected working.\n\nFEEDBACK\n7:10; analog with minute on 10, hour near 5.","explain":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific mathematical error, then show the corrected working.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justifi